sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Planarian flatworms exposed to barium, a nonspecific potassium channel blocker, lose their heads but soon regenerate new heads completely adapted to barium, and transcriptomic analysis shows only a handful of genes up- or down-regulated, which Levin interprets as cells solving a problem in high-dimensional transcriptional space without an evolved response to barium.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Planarian heads degenerated by barium regenerate adapted to it via a handful of genes";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Intelligence Below the Cellular Level › The Inner Life of Active Matter”. Scope: Planarian flatworms exposed to barium chloride (author's lab's prior work, ref [66])"
}
